        "original_id": "02831d93-d5e0-59c7-8c87-7f510d732b0e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Howard Ashman, Alan Menken\n- Products: \"Little Shop of Horrors\", \"Beauty and the Beast\", \"Be Our Guest\"\n- Companies: Walt Disney Pictures\n- Roles: lyricist, composer, playwright, director\n\nFacts:\n- Howard Elliott Ashman was born on May 17, 1950, and he was an American playwright and lyricist.\n- In 1982, Howard Ashman again directed and wrote both the book and lyrics for the musical \"Little Shop of Horrors\".\n- \"Little Shop of Horrors\" became a long-running success and led to a 1986 feature film.\n- Howard Ashman died on March 14, 1991.\n- In 1991, Walt Disney Pictures released \"Beauty and the Beast\" as its 30th animated feature film.\n- Howard Ashman and Alan Menken wrote the song \"Be Our Guest\" for Walt Disney Pictures' animated film \"Beauty and the Beast\"; Ashman was the lyricist and Menken was the composer.",
